mas (schemas.ts) as single normalisation path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One normalisation path for every provider: 'F12' \u2192 12, bad enums \u2192 defaults, one malformed array item dropped instead of the whole response."}, {"id": "docs_models_wire_schema", "label": "Strict wire schemas (wire.ts) for structured outputs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_models_retry_policy", "label": "Retry policy: schema error retry, length doubling, LlmError on refusal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_models_usage_tracking", "label": "Per-role usage and cost tracking (runs.stats.byRole, pricing.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_models_mockllmclient", "label": "MockLlmClient offline mode (DELTA_MOCK_LLM=1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_models_facts_vs_inference", "label": "Facts vs inference prompt rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extraction forbids inferring intent; inference happens only in synthesis where every hypothesis update must cite fact ids."}, {"id": "docs_models_quoteisverbatim", "label": "quoteIsVerbatim() verbatim-quote enforcement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Normalizes whitespace and quote characters; requires exact or \u226585% 3-word-shingle match; non-verbatim facts dropped and logged so the UI can claim every fact is backed by the page."}, {"id": "docs_models_stable_ids", "label": "Stable citable ids (F12, H3, Q2, E5)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prior facts/hypotheses/questions/events rendered with stable ids so the model can cite them; returned ids validated, unknown ids dropped with a warning."}, {"id": "docs_models_confidence_moves_with_evidence", "label": "Confidence moves with evidence (capped per-run, never 1.0)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Synthesis prompt caps per-run movement, forbids 1.0, and asks for alternative explanations and counter-evidence."}, {"id": "docs_models_revision_not_deletion", "label": "Revision, not deletion (supersedesId)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When evidence contradicts a hypothesis and supports a better reading, the model emits 'revised'; the old row is retired, new row inserted with supersedesId, both keep history."}, {"id": "docs_models_user_corrections_authoritative", "label": "User corrections are authoritative in the next synthesis prompt", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/models.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A correction stored on a hypothesis is injected as 'USER CORRECTION (authoritative, must be respected)'."}, {"id": "docs_mode